" vimrc for Obsidian's Vim mode, read by the community plugin Vimrc Support (obsidian-vimrc-support).
" Source: dotfiles-windows/obsidian/vimrc. Its install.ps1 copies it to <vault>/.obsidian.vimrc and
" overwrites the copy, so edit the source. The plugin reads it once per Obsidian window: restart
" Obsidian after a change. Ctrl+h/j/k/l (move between splits) are hotkeys in obsidian/hotkeys.json.

" Shift+h / Shift+l: previous / next tab in the same tab group, like the buffers in LazyVim
exmap tabPrev obcommand workspace:previous-tab
exmap tabNext obcommand workspace:next-tab
nmap H :tabPrev<CR>
nmap L :tabNext<CR>

" Space as the leader key, like LazyVim. Vim reads these lines in the editor (normal mode); the
" plugin dotfiles-vim reads the same exmap and nmap <Space> lines for the file explorer, reading view
" and the new-tab page, so add keys here only (as exmap ... obcommand ... and nmap <Space>... :name<CR>).
" Obsidian's Vim has no <leader> or mapleader, so the keys say <Space>. Space moves right by default,
" and a key that fully matches runs at once even when a longer mapping starts with it, so that
" default goes first (unmap without a mode: the default has none, so nunmap would not find it).
" The keys pressed so far show next to the mode in the status bar (plugins/dotfiles-vim).
unmap <Space>
exmap findFile obcommand switcher:open
exmap grep obcommand global-search:open
exmap explorer obcommand file-explorer:reveal-active-file
exmap commands obcommand command-palette:open
exmap outline obcommand outline:open-for-current
exmap closeTab obcommand workspace:close
exmap splitDown obcommand workspace:split-horizontal
exmap splitRight obcommand workspace:split-vertical
" Find Files: the quick switcher lists the recent files until you type (also LazyVim's <leader>fr)
nmap <Space><Space> :findFile<CR>
" Grep: the search pane in the left sidebar
nmap <Space>/ :grep<CR>
" Explorer: the file explorer, with the current note selected
nmap <Space>e :explorer<CR>
" Commands (LazyVim's <leader>: is the command history; Obsidian has none)
nmap <Space>sC :commands<CR>
nmap <Space>: :commands<CR>
" Symbols: the outline (headings) of the current note
nmap <Space>ss :outline<CR>
" Delete buffer: close the tab
nmap <Space>bd :closeTab<CR>
" Split below / right
nmap <Space>- :splitDown<CR>
nmap <Space>| :splitRight<CR>
